  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "If $X∼B(11,0.65),$  then, **rounded to $3$ decimal places**, $P(X\\le 10)≈${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(11,0.65),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{11}{x}){(0.65)}^{x}{(0.35)}^{11-x}.\n$$\n\nComputing $P(X\\le 10)$ will require us to compute $f(x)$ at $x=0,1,2,3,…,10.$ However, if we compute the complement $P(X>10)$ instead, then we will only have to compute $f(x)$ at $x=11,$ which will result in a much faster computation.\n\nComputing $P(X>10),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>10) & =P(X\\in \\{11\\}) \\\\  & =f(11) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{11}{11}){(0.65)}^{11}{(0.35)}^{11-11} \\\\  & =1{(0.65)}^{11}{(0.35)}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.009\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 10) & =1-P(X>10) \\\\  & ≈1-0.009 \\\\  & =0.991\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
